{"name":"Deep Sea Base","hex":"#2c2c57","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"deep","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Extending, reaching or positioned far from a point of reference, especially downwards.\nExtending far down from the top, or surface, to the bottom, literally or figuratively.","Extending far down from the top, or surface, to the bottom, literally or figuratively."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Far, especially far down through something or into something, physically or figuratively.","In a profound, not superficial, manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deep"},{"term":"sea","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Semai."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large body of salt water.","The ocean; the continuous body of salt water covering a majority of the Earth's surface."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sea"},{"term":"base","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something from which other things extend; a foundation.\n A supporting, lower or bottom component of a structure or object.","A supporting, lower or bottom component of a structure or object."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To give as its foundation or starting point; to lay the foundation of.","To be located (at a particular place)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/base"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sea Base","blocks":[{"text":"Sea Base, formerly known as Florida National High Adventure Sea Base, is a high adventure base run by Scouting America in the Florida Keys. Its counterparts are Philmont Scout Ranch in northern New Mexico; Northern Tier in Ely, Minnesota, as well as Manitoba and Ontario in Canada; and Summit Bechtel Reserve near the New River Gorge National Park in southern West Virginia."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/83/Scouting_America_Sea_Base_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea_Base"},{"title":"Deep sea","blocks":[{"text":"The deep sea is broadly defined as the ocean depth where light begins to fade, at an approximate depth of 200 m (660 ft) or the point of transition from continental shelves to continental slopes. Conditions within the deep sea are a combination of low temperatures, darkness, and high pressure. The deep sea is considered the least explored Earth biome as the extreme conditions make the environment difficult to access and explore."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Schematic_representation_of_pelagic_and_benthic_zones.jpg/330px-Schematic_representation_of_pelagic_and_benthic_zones.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deep_sea"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/BEC_Seabase_Sign.jpg/500px-BEC_Seabase_Sign.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/BEC_Seabase_Sign.jpg/1280px-BEC_Seabase_Sign.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/BEC_Seabase_Sign.jpg/500px-BEC_Seabase_Sign.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail"